  "id": "fast-steps-slopes-glitch",
  "name": "Fast steps slopes glitch: step-ups into a low ceiling, kept alive by jump spam",
  "tech": "fast-steps-slopes-glitch",
  "techNote": "The 64x32 slope of fast-steps-slopes under a ceiling that follows it 78 u over every step (the dot's 72-tall hitbox fits). A step-up teleports the dot to the next step's top + 36, which puts the hitbox's top 28 u into the ceiling over the step it came from: past squishDistance (-20), and after SquishGraceFrames (4) squished ticks Movement kills it (onDeath). Held right alone, the first step-up dies on tick 27. Pressing jump every other tick keeps it alive: each jump sets the normal collider to the dash collider (41x54, offset 0: its top 11 u lower), so the overlap stays under the squish distance, and the dot climbs the whole slope in the ceiling to the platform past its end, where the finish box is.",
